column13:
1) the original budget was for using 4 animals and we had only used 3 animals so far;
2) delays due to shutting down research and hiring activities due to COVID-19 pandemic;
3) delays due to relocation and restarting research lab with newly hired staff who required onboarding and training on research methods; 
4) the original budget included salaries for two co-investigators from the University of Chicago, which was the original grantee institution;
5) delays due to UW’s financial transformation that affected hiring and purchasing;
6) delays due to backlog in UW Facilities’ services needed to renovate lab space to accommodate installation of required equipment for the research.

column41:
PI has submitted the request through the sponsor system eGCM for approval (pending OSP review/submission). The below information was included in that request; 

We kindly request a no-cost extension of IMLS Grant RE-252303-OLS-22 until December 30, 2024. As we indicated in our performance report in October 2023, we experienced a two-month delay in starting the project due to graduate administration and union guidelines. Furthermore, our research team experienced a significant response from the community that added more respondents to our research and identified a new category of participants: Neurodivergent Supervisors. This led to great findings from phase 1 but required more time to complete interviews and analysis. We also received many requests for talks and webinars across national library systems for immediate impact. We are on target for our first workshop at ALA this summer. We piloted our survey instrument and made the necessary modifications. We are confident that we can complete our work and release our toolkit by December 2024.
Please review the revised schedule. The violet bars indicate actual progress, and the light blue bars indicate our updated schedule.
